<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Earnings Call Alpha</title>
<meta name="description" content="Segment-level earnings-call sentiment tested against abnormal returns across {{ n_calls }} real transcripts.">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Source+Serif+4:ital,wght@0,400;0,600;0,700;1,400&family=IBM+Plex+Sans:wght@400;500;600&family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@400;500;600&display=swap">
<style>
  :root {
    --paper: #f4f5f3;
    --paper-raised: #ffffff;
    --ink: #1c2226;
    --ink-soft: #4a545c;
    --ink-faint: #7c868d;
    --line: #d7dbd6;
    --line-soft: #e7e9e5;
    --accent: #1b4b6b;
    --accent-soft: #dde8ee;
    --accent-strong: #123449;
    --pos: #1a7a4c;
    --neg: #a4383a;
    color-scheme: light dark;
  }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    :root {
      --paper: #14181b; --paper-raised: #1b2124; --ink: #eef0ee;
      --ink-soft: #b7c0c4; --ink-faint: #7e8a8f; --line: #333c3f;
      --line-soft: #262e31; --accent: #6fa8c9; --accent-soft: #1f3441;
      --accent-strong: #9cc5df; --pos: #5cc98c; --neg: #e28486;
    }
  }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  html, body { margin: 0; padding: 0; }
  body {
    background: var(--paper); color: var(--ink);
    font-family: 'IBM Plex Sans', -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', sans-serif;
    font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.6;
  }
  h1, h2, h3 { font-family: 'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif; color: var(--ink); text-wrap: balance; font-weight: 600; margin: 0; }
  a { color: var(--accent); }
  .shell { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 240px minmax(0, 780px); gap: 0 56px; justify-content: center; max-width: 1180px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 40px 24px 120px; }
  nav.rail { position: sticky; top: 40px; align-self: start; height: max-content; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 18px; }
  .rail-mark { font-family: 'Source Serif 4', serif; font-size: 1.05rem; font-weight: 600; line-height: 1.3; }
  .rail-mark small { display: block; font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; font-size: 0.7rem; letter-spacing: 0.06em; color: var(--ink-faint); font-weight: 400; margin-top: 4px; }
  .rail-links { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 2px; margin-top: 8px; }
  .rail-links a { color: var(--ink-soft); text-decoration: none; font-size: 0.86rem; padding: 6px 10px; border-radius: 6px; }
  .rail-links a:hover { color: var(--ink); background: var(--line-soft); }
  .rail-verdict { margin-top: 6px; padding: 14px; border-radius: 10px; background: var(--paper-raised); border: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .rail-verdict .lbl { font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; font-size: 0.66rem; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-faint); }
  .rail-verdict .val { font-family: 'Source Serif 4', serif; font-size: 1.05rem; font-weight: 600; margin-top: 4px; color: var(--neg); }
  .rail-verdict .sub { font-size: 0.78rem; color: var(--ink-soft); margin-top: 6px; }
  main { min-width: 0; }
  header.masthead { padding-bottom: 28px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); margin-bottom: 40px; }
  .kicker { font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; font-size: 0.72rem; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--accent); margin-bottom: 10px; }
  h1.title { font-size: 2.1rem; line-height: 1.15; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .dek { color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 1.05rem; max-width: 62ch; }
  .meta-row { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; margin-top: 20px; }
  .chip { font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; font-size: 0.72rem; padding: 5px 10px; border-radius: 999px; border: 1px solid var(--line); color: var(--ink-soft); background: var(--paper-raised); }
  section { margin-bottom: 52px; scroll-margin-top: 24px; }
  section .eyebrow { font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; font-size: 0.72rem; letter-spacing: 0.09em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--accent); margin-bottom: 8px; }
  section h2 { font-size: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 16px; }
  section p { max-width: 68ch; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  section p + p { margin-top: 12px; }
  section p strong { color: var(--ink); }
  .callout { background: var(--paper-raised); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-left: 3px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 0 10px 10px 0; padding: 18px 20px; margin: 18px 0; }
  .callout p { color: var(--ink); max-width: none; }
  .callout .h { font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; font-size: 0.7rem; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--accent); margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .tiles { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(150px, 1fr)); gap: 1px; background: var(--line); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px; overflow: hidden; margin: 20px 0; }
  .tile { background: var(--paper-raised); padding: 16px 18px; }
  .tile .k { font-size: 0.72rem; color: var(--ink-faint); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.06em; font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; }
  .tile .v { font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; font-size: 1.5rem; margin-top: 4px; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .tile .v.neg { color: var(--neg); }
  .tile .v.pos { color: var(--pos); }
  .tile .d { font-size: 0.76rem; color: var(--ink-soft); margin-top: 4px; }
  .chart-card { background: var(--paper-raised); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 12px; padding: 20px 22px 16px; margin: 20px 0; }
  .chart-card .chart-title { font-size: 0.95rem; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 2px; }
  .chart-card .chart-sub { font-size: 0.78rem; color: var(--ink-faint); margin-bottom: 14px; }
  svg text { fill: var(--ink-soft); font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; }
  .legend { display: flex; gap: 18px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: 10px; font-size: 0.75rem; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .legend span { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; }
  .swatch { width: 10px; height: 10px; border-radius: 3px; display: inline-block; }
  .tbl-wrap { overflow-x: auto; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px; }
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 0.86rem; background: var(--paper-raised); }
  thead th { text-align: left; font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; font-size: 0.68rem; letter-spacing: 0.05em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-faint); padding: 10px 14px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); white-space: nowrap; }
  tbody td { padding: 9px 14px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-soft); font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; white-space: nowrap; }
  tbody td.name { font-family: 'IBM Plex Sans', sans-serif; font-variant-numeric: normal; white-space: normal; }
  tbody tr:last-child td { border-bottom: none; }
  .sector-badge { font-size: 0.68rem; padding: 2px 7px; border-radius: 5px; background: var(--accent-soft); color: var(--accent-strong); }
  details.call-detail { border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px; background: var(--paper-raised); overflow: hidden; }
  details.call-detail summary { cursor: pointer; padding: 12px 16px; list-style: none; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 12px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  details.call-detail summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
  .sum-left { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px; }
  .sum-ticker { font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; font-weight: 600; font-size: 0.9rem; min-width: 46px; }
  .sum-date { font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--ink-faint); font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; }
  .call-detail img { display: block; width: 100%; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); background: #fff; }
  .sum-dispersion { font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; font-size: 0.78rem; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .lim-list { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px; margin-top: 16px; }
  .lim-item { display: flex; gap: 14px; }
  .lim-num { font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; font-size: 0.75rem; color: var(--ink-faint); padding-top: 2px; min-width: 20px; }
  .lim-body p { margin: 0; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 0.92rem; }
  .lim-body strong { color: var(--ink); }
  footer.colophon { margin-top: 60px; padding-top: 22px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); font-size: 0.78rem; color: var(--ink-faint); display: flex; justify-content: space-between; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 10px; }
  @media (max-width: 880px) {
    .shell { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    nav.rail { position: static; flex-direction: row; overflow-x: auto; padding-bottom: 8px; }
    .rail-links { flex-direction: row; }
    .rail-verdict { display: none; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="shell">
  <nav class="rail">
    <div class="rail-mark">Earnings Call Alpha<small>SEGMENT-SENTIMENT RESEARCH NOTE</small></div>
    <div class="rail-links">
      <a href="#hypothesis">Hypothesis</a>
      <a href="#method">Method</a>
      <a href="#sample">Sample</a>
      <a href="#regression">Regression test</a>
      <a href="#backtest">Backtest</a>
      <a href="#calls">Per-call detail</a>
      <a href="#limits">Limitations</a>
    </div>
    <div class="rail-verdict">
      <div class="lbl">Current verdict, n&#8201;=&#8201;{{ n_calls }}</div>
      {% if has_regression %}
      <div class="val">H1 not supported</div>
      <div class="sub">Dispersion's p-value is {{ regression_fmt['1d'].pvalue }} (1d) / {{ regression_fmt['3d'].pvalue }} (3d) &mdash; not distinguishable from zero.</div>
      {% else %}
      <div class="val">Sample too small</div>
      <div class="sub">n={{ n_calls }} is below the regression test's own n&ge;10 threshold; no verdict yet.</div>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
  </nav>

  <main>
    <header class="masthead">
      <div class="kicker">Reproduction &amp; extension &middot; arXiv:2505.16090, arXiv:2410.01772</div>
      <h1 class="title">Does segment-level sentiment beat whole-transcript sentiment?</h1>
      <p class="dek">A falsifiable test on {{ n_calls }} real, first-party earnings-call transcripts: whether the dispersion of FinBERT sentiment across a call's Q&amp;A segments predicts abnormal returns beyond what the whole-transcript average already explains.</p>
      <div class="meta-row">
        <span class="chip">n = {{ n_calls }} calls</span>
        <span class="chip">{{ n_tickers }} tickers &middot; {{ n_sectors }} sectors</span>
        <span class="chip">{{ tickers_list }}</span>
        <span class="chip">FinBERT &middot; Fama-French &middot; PSR</span>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section id="hypothesis">
      <div class="eyebrow">01 &middot; Hypothesis</div>
      <h2>A falsifiable claim, stated before looking at results</h2>
      <p><strong>H1:</strong> the dispersion of sentiment across a call's segments (max&nbsp;&minus;&nbsp;min segment sentiment) has incremental predictive power for the 1-day and 3-day abnormal return around the call, beyond what whole-transcript sentiment alone explains.</p>
      <div class="callout">
        <div class="h">Why this, not another metric</div>
        <p>Most quant portfolios show price-only signals; most IB-style analyses show no statistical validation. This sits between the two &mdash; a qualitative artifact (an earnings call) tested with a quant-style falsifiable claim, explicit backtest, and transaction costs. A null result here is treated as a complete, reportable finding, not a failed run.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="method">
      <div class="eyebrow">02 &middot; Method</div>
      <h2>Six steps, each independently auditable</h2>
      <p>1&#8201;&middot;&#8201;<strong>Segment</strong> each call into prepared-remarks blocks and analyst Q&amp;A exchanges (rule-based, not learned). 2&#8201;&middot;&#8201;<strong>Score</strong> each segment with FinBERT. 3&#8201;&middot;&#8201;<strong>Compute</strong> whole-transcript sentiment, segment dispersion, and core-segment sentiment. 4&#8201;&middot;&#8201;<strong>Measure</strong> Fama-French market-model abnormal returns for [0,+1] and [0,+3] trading days. 5&#8201;&middot;&#8201;<strong>Test</strong> with a nested regression isolating dispersion's incremental R&sup2;. 6&#8201;&middot;&#8201;<strong>Backtest</strong> a walk-forward long/short sort, scored with the Probabilistic Sharpe Ratio.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="sample">
      <div class="eyebrow">03 &middot; Sample</div>
      <h2>{{ n_calls }} calls, sourced first-party only</h2>
      <p>Every transcript is either an SEC 8-K exhibit or a PDF/HTML transcript published directly by the company's own investor-relations site &mdash; never a third-party aggregator.</p>
      <div class="tbl-wrap">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Ticker</th><th>Sector</th><th>Calls</th><th># in sample</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
          {% for r in sample_rows %}
            <tr><td class="name">{{ r.ticker }}</td><td><span class="sector-badge">{{ r.sector }}</span></td><td>{{ r.dates }}</td><td>{{ r.n }}</td></tr>
          {% endfor %}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="regression">
      <div class="eyebrow">04 &middot; Regression test</div>
      {% if has_regression %}
      <h2>H1 is not supported at this sample size</h2>
      <p>A nested OLS regression compares whole-transcript sentiment alone against whole-transcript sentiment&nbsp;+&nbsp;dispersion. The number that matters is the <em>incremental</em> R&sup2; dispersion adds, and whether its coefficient clears significance.</p>
      <div class="tiles">
        <div class="tile"><div class="k">1d p-value</div><div class="v">{{ regression_fmt['1d'].pvalue }}</div><div class="d">n={{ regression_fmt['1d'].n }}</div></div>
        <div class="tile"><div class="k">3d p-value</div><div class="v">{{ regression_fmt['3d'].pvalue }}</div><div class="d">n={{ regression_fmt['3d'].n }}</div></div>
        <div class="tile"><div class="k">Incremental R&sup2; (1d)</div><div class="v">{{ regression_fmt['1d'].incremental_r2 }}</div><div class="d">over whole-transcript alone</div></div>
        <div class="tile"><div class="k">Incremental R&sup2; (3d)</div><div class="v">{{ regression_fmt['3d'].incremental_r2 }}</div><div class="d">over whole-transcript alone</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="callout">
        <div class="h">Reading this honestly</div>
        <p>Neither p-value is close to conventional significance thresholds, even before any multiple-testing correction. This is reported as the finding, not smoothed over &mdash; see the project README for how this number changed as the sample grew.</p>
      </div>
      {% else %}
      <h2>Not enough calls yet to run the test</h2>
      <p>The nested regression requires n&ge;10 calls; this sample currently has {{ n_calls }}. Add more transcripts and re-render to see the actual result here.</p>
      {% endif %}
    </section>

    <section id="backtest">
      <div class="eyebrow">05 &middot; Illustrative backtest</div>
      {% if has_backtest %}
      <h2>Walk-forward long/short, scored honestly</h2>
      <p>A signal-sorted long/short backtest with 10bps/side transaction costs and a walk-forward split. Scored with the Probabilistic Sharpe Ratio (Bailey &amp; Lopez de Prado, 2012) rather than a raw Sharpe ratio.</p>
      <div class="tiles">
        <div class="tile"><div class="k">Trades</div><div class="v">{{ backtest_fmt.n_trades }}</div><div class="d">out-of-sample</div></div>
        <div class="tile"><div class="k">Cumulative return</div><div class="v {{ 'neg' if backtest.cumulative_return < 0 else 'pos' }}">{{ backtest_fmt.cumulative_return }}</div><div class="d">net of costs</div></div>
        <div class="tile"><div class="k">Raw Sharpe</div><div class="v {{ 'neg' if backtest.sharpe_per_trade_raw < 0 else 'pos' }}">{{ backtest_fmt.sharpe_raw }}</div><div class="d">per-trade</div></div>
        <div class="tile"><div class="k">Probabilistic Sharpe</div><div class="v {{ 'neg' if backtest.probabilistic_sharpe_ratio < 0.5 else 'pos' }}">{{ backtest_fmt.psr }}</div><div class="d">P(true Sharpe &gt; 0)</div></div>
      </div>
      {% if equity_points %}
      <div class="chart-card">
        <div class="chart-title">Cumulative net return, walk-forward order</div>
        <div class="chart-sub">{{ equity_points|length }} out-of-sample trades, sorted by call date</div>
        {% set min_v = equity_points|map(attribute='cum_pct')|min %}
        {% set max_v = equity_points|map(attribute='cum_pct')|max %}
        {% set span = (max_v - min_v) if (max_v - min_v) > 0.01 else 1 %}
        {% set n = equity_points|length %}
        <svg viewBox="0 0 640 200" role="img" aria-label="Line chart of cumulative net backtest return across {{ n }} trades">
          <line x1="50" y1="20" x2="50" y2="160" stroke="var(--line)" stroke-width="1"/>
          <line x1="50" y1="160" x2="610" y2="160" stroke="var(--line)" stroke-width="1"/>
          <text x="42" y="24" text-anchor="end" font-size="10">{{ "%.0f"|format(max_v) }}%</text>
          <text x="42" y="164" text-anchor="end" font-size="10">{{ "%.0f"|format(min_v) }}%</text>
          <polyline points="{% for p in equity_points %}{{ 80 + (p.i * (500 / ([n-1,1]|max))) | round(1) }},{{ (160 - ((p.cum_pct - min_v) / span) * 130) | round(1) }}{% if not loop.last %} {% endif %}{% endfor %}" fill="none" stroke="var(--neg)" stroke-width="2.5"/>
          {% for p in equity_points %}
          <circle cx="{{ 80 + (p.i * (500 / ([n-1,1]|max))) | round(1) }}" cy="{{ (160 - ((p.cum_pct - min_v) / span) * 130) | round(1) }}" r="3.5" fill="var(--neg)"/>
          {% endfor %}
        </svg>
      </div>
      {% endif %}
      {% else %}
      <h2>Not enough calls yet for a walk-forward trade</h2>
      <p>{{ backtest.note }}</p>
      {% endif %}
    </section>

    <section id="calls">
      <div class="eyebrow">06 &middot; Per-call detail</div>
      <h2>Every call, whole-transcript vs. core-segment sentiment</h2>
      <p>Click a row to see that call's full segment-sentiment heatmap.</p>

      <div class="chart-card">
        <div class="chart-title">Whole-transcript vs. core-segment sentiment, all {{ n_calls }} calls</div>
        <div class="chart-sub">FinBERT score range &minus;1 to +1</div>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 660 {{ 24 + calls|length * 27 }}" role="img" aria-label="Diverging bar chart comparing whole-transcript sentiment to core-segment sentiment for each call">
          <line x1="330" y1="10" x2="330" y2="{{ 14 + calls|length * 27 }}" stroke="var(--line)" stroke-width="1"/>
          {% for c in calls %}
          {% set y = 14 + loop.index0 * 27 %}
          <text x="8" y="{{ y + 15 }}" font-size="10.5" font-family="'IBM Plex Sans', sans-serif">{{ c.ticker }} {{ c.date }}</text>
          <rect x="{{ 330 + c.whole_bar.x }}" y="{{ y }}" width="{{ c.whole_bar.width }}" height="9" fill="var(--ink-faint)"/>
          {% if c.core_bar %}
          <rect x="{{ 330 + c.core_bar.x }}" y="{{ y + 11 }}" width="{{ c.core_bar.width }}" height="9" fill="var(--accent)"/>
          {% endif %}
          {% endfor %}
        </svg>
        <div class="legend"><span><span class="swatch" style="background:var(--ink-faint)"></span>Whole-transcript</span><span><span class="swatch" style="background:var(--accent)"></span>Core-segment</span></div>
      </div>

      {% for c in calls %}
      <details class="call-detail">
        <summary>
          <span class="sum-left"><span class="sum-ticker">{{ c.ticker }}</span><span class="sum-date">{{ c.date }}</span></span>
          <span class="sum-dispersion">dispersion {{ "%.2f"|format(c.dispersion) if c.dispersion is not none else "—" }}{% if c.gap is not none %} &middot; core&minus;whole {{ "%+.2f"|format(c.gap) }}{% endif %}</span>
        </summary>
        <img src="{{ c.heatmap_img }}" alt="Segment sentiment heatmap for {{ c.ticker }} {{ c.date }}" loading="lazy">
      </details>
      {% endfor %}
    </section>

    <section id="limits">
      <div class="eyebrow">07 &middot; Limitations, stated up front</div>
      <h2>What this is not</h2>
      <div class="lim-list">
        <div class="lim-item"><div class="lim-num">01</div><div class="lim-body"><p><strong>Small, non-random sample.</strong> {{ n_calls }} calls across {{ n_tickers }} tickers, curated for transcript availability &mdash; not a random draw from the market.</p></div></div>
        <div class="lim-item"><div class="lim-num">02</div><div class="lim-body"><p><strong>No multiple-testing correction</strong> across the two return windows tested (1-day, 3-day).</p></div></div>
        <div class="lim-item"><div class="lim-num">03</div><div class="lim-body"><p><strong>Core-segment keywords use present-day knowledge</strong> of each firm's largest business line, which may not match an older quarter.</p></div></div>
        <div class="lim-item"><div class="lim-num">04</div><div class="lim-body"><p><strong>Daily closes, not intraday.</strong> Event-window returns are coarser than sub-minute market-microstructure studies.</p></div></div>
        <div class="lim-item"><div class="lim-num">05</div><div class="lim-body"><p><strong>Research prototype</strong>, not a claim of a deployable trading signal.</p></div></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <footer class="colophon">
      <span>Reproduces Kim et al. 2025 (arXiv:2505.16090) &amp; DeFine (arXiv:2410.01772)</span>
      <span>src/site/render.py &middot; n={{ n_calls }}</span>
    </footer>
  </main>
</div>
</body>
</html>
